    "note": "Public Chapter 727 (2018-04-19), the law as enacted, printed as Senate Bill 1697 substituted for House Bill 1512. Section 38-6-105 is replaced in full; the retired commission card part is not a gun rule. Marginal gun_policy: a narrow public-employee firearm retention rule."
  },
  "operative_text": "SECTION 1 (TCA 38-6-105): After twenty-five (25) years of honorable service by an agent or uniformed law enforcement officer of the bureau, in recognition of the agent's or uniformed law enforcement office/s many years of good and faithful public service, the bureau shall authorize the agent or uniformed law enforcement officer to retain the agent's or uniformed law enforcement office/s service weapon.\nSECTION 1 (TCA 38-6-105): Cards issued under this provision shall bear the inscription, in print of equal or larger size than the rest of the printing on the card, the words \"Not a handgun permit.\""
